__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
.venv/
# Worker-writable hot state, shared via the primary checkout and NEVER committed: the
# claim files, the merge-slot lease, telemetry, and the markdown backend's live records.
# The tracked artefacts are written by the orchestrator once per wave, not by whoever
# happens to hold a claim — a tracked file written mid-wave leaves the primary checkout
# dirty and fails the next wave's pre-flight.
#
# `.harness/stacks/` and `.harness/frameworks/` are NOT ignored: those are project config
# a repository writes on purpose, and they must travel with it.
**/.harness/run/
**/.harness/tasks/

# The independence reviews: valuable history for this repository, and noise for
# anyone installing the plugin. Kept locally, never shipped.
independence_check.md

# Feature proposals: the argument for a change, written before it is built. Local for
# now — not shipped to anyone installing the plugin, and not yet committed here either.
proposals/

# This repository's OWN prompts, for engineering the harness rather than using it. The
# plugin's command surface is `commands/` at its root; `.claude/commands/` is where a
# project keeps its own, which is why `resolve._prompts_dir` falls back to exactly here.
# Ignored rather than merely untracked: distribution is a clone of this repo, so
# `git add -A` is all it would take to ship four dev commands into every consumer's cache.
.claude/
